# Plan step commit summaries

When you finish implementing a step of a plan created in this repo:

- Do not create a git commit, stage files, or run `git commit` unless the user explicitly asks you to commit in that message.
- End the step with a commit summary they can copy-paste. Match this repository's short title-plus-why style (one title line, optional one-sentence body).
- Put the summary in a fenced code block so it is easy to copy.

```markdown
# BAD
git commit -m "Specify diagnostic response caching"

# GOOD
Finish the step, then give:

Specify diagnostic response caching without implementing it

Document how DiagnosticService should reuse a DiagnosticLog for the same session car, track, and deficit set.
```
